Landscape touch looks good. Materials visible. Labels centered and no key overlap. Controls at bottom. The dock overlays underground not action. Good.

Potential improvement: the end turn button and fire button overlap? No, separate rows (end turn at y280, fire at y342). Fine.

Now portrait materials. Let's implement dock relocation. Need be cautious with updateHud references and event binding: buttons are bound via `$$('.mat')` at startup; moving DOM preserves listeners. Good.

Add HTML: inside hud-top after scoreboard:
```
<div id="materialsDock" class="materials-dock hidden" aria-label="Materials"></div>
```
But hud-top flex; hidden by default. In portrait, show.

JS:
```
const materialsSlot = $('#materials');
const materialsDock = $('#materialsDock');
const operatorCard = $('.operator-card');
let materialsInDock=null;
function layoutHudExtras(){
 const compact = window.matchMedia('(max-width: 700px) and (orientation: portrait)').matches;
 if(compact === materialsInDock) return;
 materialsInDock=compact;
 if(compact){ materialsDock.appendChild(materialsSlot); materialsDock.classList.remove('hidden'); }
 else { operatorCard.appendChild(materialsSlot); materialsDock.classList.add('hidden'); }
}
```
Call on resize (existing listener `updateRotateHint` could call), at init. But operatorCard append puts materials at bottom after operator-top, which is its original place anyway. Good.

However `layoutHudExtras` uses `isTouch`; on desktop narrow portrait (browser window 400x800) compact? We can apply only if `isTouch` OR width<700, but if no touch, HUD is desktop and operator hidden by max-width 860; materials also needed. Better show dock whenever `max-width:700px and portrait` regardless of touch. It's okay.

CSS:
```
.materials-dock { display:none; }
@media (max-width:700px) {
 .materials-dock:not(.hidden) { display:flex; width:100%; order:4; }
 .materials-dock .materials { margin:0; width:100%; gap:6px; }
}
```
HUD-top flex-wrap at max-width980, order 3 scoreboard; materials order4. Width 100%. It appears next to? `flex-basis:100%`.

But if `#materials` is moved, desktop operator card has no `.materials` after a resize to portrait then back? JS moves it back. Fine.

In portrait screenshot, HUD top turn+wind, then materials dock row below at ~100, then battlefield. The toast top at 104 could overlap materials; toast only transient. Set toast top 140 in portrait maybe.

Let's implement.

